26.11.144	Restart and Switch off have moved from Settings to a panel you drag down from the top of the screen, which can also turn the screen off. Settings has a new Services tab, for apps that run in the background.
26.11.142	In the dark, a tap on the screen lights it for a moment instead of pressing what's underneath.
26.11.138	Settings shows each stage of an update as it goes, with a bar that fills while it checks, downloads and installs.
26.11.134	The Shop is here, on the home screen. Everything in it is free: tap Get to install an app, and its tile appears on the home screen.
26.11.128	The bar shows a download arrow when updates are waiting to install, and the Updates tab in Settings gets a dot.
26.11.128	Tap the clock to open Settings at Display, where its format is set.
26.11.128	A tap on the dark screen brings back the screensaver if it was showing, for a quick look at the time.
26.11.128	The screen's settings file on the boot volume is now settings/interface.txt; yours is moved over by itself.
26.11.117	The OpenFrame starts with its bird all the way from the first logo to the home screen, which fades in from it.
26.11.114	Until the OpenFrame has set its clock from the internet after a start, the clock shows 00:00 rather than a wrong time.
26.11.108	A flip clock screensaver comes on after five minutes untouched; change or turn it off in Settings, Display.
26.11.105	Settings, Display can now turn the screen off after a while untouched. A tap turns it back on.
26.11.102	Settings, About now shows this OpenFrame's details at a glance: its model, firmware, memory, storage, and a Crystal HD card if it has one.
26.11.89	The bar now has a speaker. Tap it to change the volume without opening Settings.
26.11.80	The Audio tab shows how a USB DAC is connected, and what it's playing at.
26.11.69	Play a test sound, left then right then both, in Settings under Audio.
26.11.65	Choose where the sound goes, a USB DAC included, in Settings under Audio.
26.11.59	Name the OpenFrame in Settings, under About.
26.11.57	The screen shows each brightness as you drag the slider.
26.11.56	Remote access can be turned off again, in Settings under Network.
26.11.53	Set how dim and how bright automatic brightness goes, and whether the screen switches off in the dark, in Settings under Display.
26.11.51	A welcome screen helps set up a new OpenFrame.
26.11.51	Choose when the OpenFrame updates itself, in Settings under Updates.
26.11.51	Sprite says when it's been updated, rather than just restarting.
26.11.44	Settings, About, can erase the OpenFrame for its next owner.
26.11.41	Settings has an Updates tab, showing what's waiting and what's new.
26.11.39	Once an hour, the OpenFrame tells openbeak.net it's running. Settings, About, says exactly what's sent.
26.11.38	A warning sign in the status bar points out a problem in the network settings files. Tap the network icons to go straight to them.
26.11.37	Tap the Wi-Fi or Ethernet line in Settings to see the network's details.
26.11.34	Settings is now in tabs down the left.
